[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known, with one fix queued. It holds two problems, and that
fix reaches only one of them. Each now has its own ticket.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The last column still says the smaller group has no ticket of its own. The table is built from the
desk's export, which does not know about the tickets below.

## The two problems

- **[Parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/jacksoncarl/support-kb-4471/issues/1).**
  A day-first tenant's dates come out flipped. This is what #4471 describes, and the queued fix is for
  this one.
- **[booking-v3 hints MM/DD/YYYY to day-first tenants](https://github.com/jacksoncarl/support-kb-4471/issues/2).**
  The form's hint tells people to type the month first, and the form then reads the date the tenant's
  way. The parser is not involved, so fixing the parser leaves these bookings wrong.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close the second ticket when the parser fix ships. Check it against reports from the booking-v3
form after the fix.
</Callout>

## How to tell them apart

Use the tenant and the channel: `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` decides. A report through the booking form of a
tenant on booking-v3 is the hint problem. Every other report from a day-first tenant is the parser
problem.

Do not use these three things:

- **The subject line.** Decision 0001 merges on it, and both problems share the same subjects.
- **The intake tag.** It is a guess from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the tenant in
  both groups.
- **The raw row count.** The export repeats some rows, so count each report id once.

The note under the table counts reports that read as a move of one day, not a flipped date. They are
counted where the tenant files them. They do not have a ticket of their own yet, and the first ticket
lists them to re-check after the parser fix.

## What this page does not change

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) stays as accepted: only a new record can replace
it. The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) belongs to the desk and is unchanged.

